.SS " None sphinx\&.writers\&.latex\&.Table\&.add_cell ( self, int height, int width)"

.PP
.nf
Adds a new cell to a table\&.

It will be located at current position: (``self\&.row``, ``self\&.col``)\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " \fBTableCell\fP | None sphinx\&.writers\&.latex\&.Table\&.cell ( self, int | None  row = \fCNone\fP, int | None  col = \fCNone\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Returns a cell object (i\&.e\&. rectangular area) containing given position\&.

If no option arguments: ``row`` or ``col`` are given, the current position;
``self\&.row`` and ``self\&.col`` are used to get a cell object by default\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " str sphinx\&.writers\&.latex\&.Table\&.get_colspec ( self)"

.PP
.nf
Returns a column spec of table\&.

This is what LaTeX calls the 'preamble argument' of the used table environment\&.

\&.\&. note::

   The ``\\\\X`` and ``T`` column type specifiers are defined in
   ``sphinxlatextables\&.sty``\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " str sphinx\&.writers\&.latex\&.Table\&.get_table_type ( self)"

.PP
.nf
Returns the LaTeX environment name for the table\&.

The class currently supports:

* longtable
* tabular
* tabulary

.fi
.PP
 
